Linux Admin Center for Debian and Ubuntu
=========================================

The Debian package installs Linux Admin Center below /usr and is managed by
apt and dpkg.

Package-managed installations intentionally do not install the lac-uninstall
command. Removing package files outside apt or dpkg would leave the package
database inconsistent.

Install a local package with:

  sudo apt install ./linux-admin-center_<version>_all.deb

Remove it with:

  sudo apt remove linux-admin-center

Configuration under /etc/lac and user configuration under ~/.config/lac are
not package-managed and are therefore preserved when the package is removed.
